                           MUI-Config for DayDream
                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

MUIConfig is an alternative configuration program for those who don't
like text files. Some of you do hate MUI, but I wrote used MUI because:

1) MUI programming is fast. It would have taken N weeks to get it done in
   gadtools.
2) MUI gives you font sensitivity and stuff.
3) MUI looks great.
4) Massive memory consumption of MUI is only temporary, this isn't running
   in the background all the time.
5) MUI has some nice features... =)


Some important things to remember if you're using MUI Config:

1) MUIConfig does NOT save changes to your configuration textfile, it 
   modifies the datafiles!!! If you start using MUIConfig, there's no
   way to use old textbased config program unless you write textfile
   by hand!!

2) Producing ESC is possible with ctrl-[key], in finland the key is
   å. Also utility like newedit could make pasting possible.

3) TAB-key is very handy if you hate mouse.

4) Saving is done via pull-down menu.

5) There's no documentation for MUIConfig yet, check out DayDream.guide for
   some kind of hints what the gadgets are about..

6) You CAN save out a commented textfile from MUIConfig.
